WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.290
In this lesson, you will learn to find and fix a mistake (a bug) in a script by watching what the character does.

2
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.610
A bug is a mistake in code.

3
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.130
It makes the character do the wrong thing.

4
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.280
Press Run and watch.

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.420
Where does the character go wrong?

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:22.130
Change one block, then run it again.

7
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.260
Did that fix it?

8
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.860
Every coder makes bugs.

9
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.750
Finding them is part of the fun!

10
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:34.110
This code has a bug: the bee goes the wrong way. Fix it so the bee reaches the flower star.

11
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:38.450
The down arrow should have been up. Bug squashed!

12
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.470
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

13
00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:45.970
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
